@event streets_chestnuts
# en: Hot Chestnuts
title [2201ad] = 烤栗子
# en: On the corner a chestnut seller's brazier glows like a little forge, and half the street has stopped to warm its hands at it. The chestnuts split and smoke in the pan. "A penny a cone," says the seller, "or mind the coals for me while I fetch another sack, and eat what you like."
text [88c946] = 街角卖栗子的炭盆烧得像个小熔炉，半条街的人都停下来烤手。栗子在锅里裂开、冒烟。“一便士一筒，”卖栗子的说，“要不就帮我看着炭火，我去再扛一袋来，你想吃多少吃多少。”
# en: A winter city street corner, a chestnut seller's glowing brazier, paper cones of roast chestnuts, a student warming their hands at the coals.
scene [fa4be8] = 冬天的城市街角，卖栗子的人炭盆烧得通红，一筒筒纸包的烤栗子，一个学生在炭火边烤手。
# en: Buy a cone
opt.left.label [0b88e3] = 买一筒
# en: You pay your penny and walk on with a hot paper cone in both hands, peeling chestnuts with your fingertips and burning your tongue on every one. For half a street the winter can't touch you.
opt.left.say.1 [45c91a] = 你付了一便士，两手捧着热乎乎的纸筒往前走，用指尖剥栗子，每一颗都烫了舌头。有半条街那么长，冬天碰不到你。
# en: Mind the brazier for him
opt.right.label [35b61e] = 替他看着炭盆
# en: You stand at the coals for half an hour, shaking the pan, selling cones and eating every third chestnut. When the seller comes back with his sack he's delighted with the takings. Your fingertips are scorched pink.
opt.right.say.1 [adf579] = 你在炭火边站了半个钟头，摇着锅，卖着纸筒，每三颗吃一颗。卖栗子的扛着袋子回来，对这份进账高兴极了。你的指尖烫得发红。

@event streets_water_cart
# en: The Water Cart
title [95500b] = 洒水车
# en: It's so hot the cobbles shimmer. Down the street comes the water cart, laying the dust with a fan of spray from a pipe at its tail, and behind it half the street is dancing in the wet: apprentices, a fishwife, two clerks with their trousers rolled, all shrieking. The driver grins down at you. "Fill her up at the pump for me after," he says, "and you can ride the tail."
text [c7f46a] = 热得石子路都在发颤。洒水车沿街驶来，车尾的管子喷出一扇水雾压住尘土，后面半条街的人都在湿地里跳舞：学徒们、一个卖鱼的女人、两个卷起裤腿的职员，个个尖叫。车夫冲你咧嘴一笑。“待会儿帮我在水泵那儿把车灌满，”他说，“就让你坐车尾。”
# en: A dusty summer city street, a horse-drawn water cart spraying the cobbles from a pierced pipe, apprentices and passers-by dancing in the spray, a student about to join them.
scene [2d5216] = 尘土飞扬的夏日城市街道，一辆马拉洒水车用打了孔的管子往石子路上喷水，学徒和路人在水雾里跳舞，一个学生正要加入他们。
# en: Run through the spray
opt.left.label [7b7e79] = 从水雾里跑过去
# en: You run through the spray with the apprentices, twice, and come out the far side soaked, cool and laughing, and skid on the wet cobbles and bark your knee, while a clerk on the pavement watches you with open envy.
opt.left.say.1 [d92abb] = 你和学徒们一起从水雾里跑过去，跑了两趟，从另一头出来，浑身湿透、凉快、笑个不停，又在湿石子路上一滑，磕破了膝盖，人行道上一个书记员毫不掩饰地羡慕地看着你。
# en: Work the pump for him
opt.right.label [78738a] = 替他压水泵
# en: You pump the cart full at the corner, stroke after stroke, in the full sun, while the horse drinks from the trough beside you. Then he lets you ride the tail once round the block, wet to the knees. Your arms ache all evening.
opt.right.say.1 [73e01e] = 你在街角顶着大太阳一下一下地压水泵把车灌满，马在你旁边的水槽里喝水。然后他让你坐在车尾绕街区转了一圈，湿到膝盖。你的胳膊酸了一整晚。

@event streets_bolting_horse
# en: The Bolting Horse
title [2f3714] = 惊马
# en: A coal wagon tips its load with a roar, and a cab horse bolts. It comes down the street with the empty cab swinging behind it like a toy, people scattering, the cabby running behind shouting. At the crossing an old woman with a basket has stopped dead in the road.
text [088371] = 一辆运煤车哗啦一声翻了货，一匹出租马车的马受了惊。它冲下街道，空车厢在身后像玩具一样甩来甩去，人群四散，车夫在后面边跑边喊。路口，一个提篮子的老妇人在路中间愣住了。
# en: A busy city street, a cab horse bolting with its empty cab swinging behind it, people scattering, an old woman frozen at a crossing, a student lunging for the bridle.
scene [4f2537] = 繁忙的城市街道，一匹拉出租马车的马拖着空车厢狂奔，人群四散，一位老妇人僵在路口，一个学生扑向马笼头。
# en: Go for the bridle
opt.left.label [eb74bb] = 去抓马笼头
# en: You catch the bridle as it passes and hang on, dragged three strides, until the horse's head comes round and it stands, shaking. The cabby arrives, wheezing thanks, and the street claps. Your shoulder will feel it tomorrow, and you don't care.
opt.left.say.1 [2636d5] = 它经过时你抓住了笼头，死死拽着，被拖了三步，直到马头转过来，它停下，浑身发抖。车夫气喘吁吁地赶来道谢，整条街都在鼓掌。你的肩膀明天会疼，可你不在乎。
# en: You get a hand to the bridle and the horse takes you off your feet and drops you in the gutter. It goes on round the corner, where a drayman stops it. You limp off with grazed palms and torn knees.
opt.left.say.2 [9ce821] = 你一只手碰到了笼头，马把你拽离地面，扔进了水沟。它接着拐过街角，被一个运货的车夫拦了下来。你一瘸一拐地走开，手掌擦破，膝盖也破了。
# en: Pull the old woman clear
opt.right.label [bea3d3] = 把老妇人拉开
# en: You get to the crossing first and pull her out of the road, basket and all, and you both go over in the gutter as the cab rattles past. She's unhurt and furious about her eggs. You've skinned both elbows.
opt.right.say.1 [963753] = 你先赶到路口，连人带篮子把她拉出马路，马车哐啷驶过时你们俩一起摔进水沟。她毫发无伤，只为她的鸡蛋大发脾气。你两只胳膊肘都蹭破了。

@event streets_pavement_artist
# en: The Pavement Artist
title [edfb79] = 人行道画家
# en: A pavement artist has spent the whole day on his knees drawing the sea in chalk, a ship in a storm so real the passers-by step round the waves. He's on the last corner. Overhead the sky has gone the colour of slate, and the first fat drop lands in his sea.
text [6b29c3] = 一个人行道画家跪了一整天，用粉笔画大海，一条船在风暴里，逼真得路人都绕着浪走。他在画最后一角。头顶的天已经变成石板色，第一颗大雨点落进了他的海里。
# en: A city pavement covered with a huge chalk drawing of a stormy sea and a ship, a chalk artist on his knees finishing a corner, dark rain clouds gathering overhead, a student watching.
scene [5de9be] = 城市人行道上铺满一幅巨大的粉笔画，画着风暴中的大海和一条船，粉笔画家跪着在补最后一角，头顶乌云密布，一个学生在旁边看。
# en: Hold your coat over the last corner
opt.left.label [54fc86] = 用外套遮住最后一角
# en: You hold your coat out over him like a tent while the rain comes down, and he finishes the last wave with chalk running off his fingers. Then the sea washes away into the gutter, all of it, and he laughs. You're wet to the skin.
opt.left.say.1 [9a7c6a] = 雨下来了，你把外套撑在他头顶，像顶帐篷，他画完最后一道浪，粉笔从手指上往下淌。然后整片海都冲进了水沟，他笑了。你湿透了。
# en: Hold off the rain with a spell
opt.right.label [fa38e1] = 用法术挡住雨
# en: You hold your hand up and the rain parts over the pavement, a dry hole in the downpour, for the whole quarter of an hour it takes him to finish. A crowd gathers in the wet to watch the dry sea. Then you let go, and it all washes away.
opt.right.say.1 [c1153b] = 你举起手，雨在人行道上方分开，大雨里一个干燥的洞，撑了他画完所需的整整一刻钟。人群冒雨聚过来看这片干的海。然后你一松手，一切都被冲走了。
# en: The spell catches the rain and drops it all at once, a bucket's worth, square on the drawing. The sea runs into the gutter in a grey stream. The artist only shrugs. "It always goes," he says. You feel awful about it all day.
opt.right.say.2 [d2dfbc] = 法术兜住了雨，又一下子全倒了下来，足有一桶，正砸在画上。海化成一道灰色的水流进了水沟。画家只是耸耸肩。“它总会没的，”他说。你一整天都觉得过意不去。

@event streets_monkey
# en: The Organ-Grinder's Monkey
title [401384] = 手风琴艺人的猴子
# en: An organ-grinder is playing a waltz on the corner, and his monkey, in a red waistcoat and a tiny cap, comes round with a tin cup. It doffs the cap to you very politely. Then it unbuttons your coat pocket with two quick fingers and is off down the street with your purse.
text [92bc13] = 一个摇手摇风琴的艺人在街角奏着华尔兹，他的猴子穿着红马甲、戴着小帽子，端着锡杯挨个讨钱。它非常有礼貌地向你脱帽致意。然后两根手指飞快地解开你外套口袋的扣子，揣着你的钱袋顺街跑了。
# en: A city street, an organ-grinder turning the handle of a barrel organ, a small monkey in a red waistcoat and cap scampering off with a coin purse, a student giving chase.
scene [5a6278] = 城市街道，一个艺人摇着手摇风琴的把手，一只穿红马甲戴小帽的小猴子抓着钱袋跑开，一个学生在后面追。
# en: Chase it
opt.left.label [96dc3a] = 追它
# en: You run it down by the cab rank, where it stops to inspect your purse, and it gives it back with an air of having been about to. The organ-grinder laughs so hard he stops playing. You walk on with your purse and a story.
opt.left.say.1 [a12688] = 你在出租马车站追上了它，它正停下来检查你的钱袋，随即把钱袋还了回来，一副本来就打算还的样子。艺人笑得停下了琴。你揣着钱袋和一个故事继续往前走。
# en: It goes up a drainpipe and along a gutter and is gone. When you get back the organ-grinder hands back your purse, lighter by a coin "for the monkey's trouble". You can't prove a thing.
opt.left.say.2 [65bf2e] = 它顺着排水管爬上去，沿着檐沟跑了，不见了。你回来时，艺人把钱袋还给你，少了一枚硬币，“给猴子的辛苦费”。你什么也证明不了。
# en: Pay the grinder for its return
opt.right.label [462aa8] = 付钱请艺人把它叫回来
# en: You put a coin in the grinder's cup, and he whistles, and the monkey comes back and drops your purse in your hand. He tells you, while it eats a nut on his shoulder, how he won it from a sailor in a card game. You're a coin poorer and know far too much about monkeys.
opt.right.say.1 [b6f5a2] = 你往艺人的杯子里放了一枚硬币，他吹了声口哨，猴子跑回来把钱袋丢进你手里。猴子蹲在他肩上吃坚果时，他告诉你他是怎么在牌局上从一个水手手里赢来它的。你少了一枚硬币，还知道了太多关于猴子的事。

@event streets_lost_child
# en: Lost in the Crowd
title [a17b34] = 走失在人群里
# en: In the thick of a market street a very old man in a coat too big for him is standing quite still and crying without making a sound, while the crowd parts round him like water round a post. Nobody stops. He's holding a paper bag of sugared almonds very tight, and he can't remember which street is his.
text [b02bd4] = 在一条集市街最拥挤的地方，一个穿着过大外套的老人一动不动地站着，无声地哭，人群像水绕过柱子一样从他身边分开。没人停下。他紧紧攥着一纸袋糖杏仁，想不起自己住哪条街了。
# en: A crowded city market street, a very old man in a too-big coat standing lost in the middle of the crowd, a student taking his arm.
scene [97da7e] = 拥挤的城市集市街，一个穿着过大外套、迷了路的老人站在人群中间，一个学生挽住他的胳膊。
# en: Take his arm and call out
opt.left.label [9bc893] = 挽着他的胳膊喊人
# en: You take his arm, almonds and all, and walk him up and down the street calling out, and he points at windows and calls too. A frantic woman, his daughter, comes running from three streets away. By the time she's done thanking you your arm aches from his weight and your sleeve is sticky with sugar.
opt.left.say.1 [e13ac0] = 你挽着他的胳膊，连同杏仁一起，沿街来回地喊，他也指着窗户跟着喊。一个慌了神的女人，他的女儿，从三条街外跑来。等她谢完你，你的胳膊被他压得发酸，袖子上全是糖。
# en: Walk him to the watch house
opt.right.label [6b0f4f] = 把他送到巡夜队岗房
# en: You take a thin, sticky hand and walk him to the watch house, where a sergeant who has clearly done this a hundred times sits him by the stove with a biscuit. He doesn't look at you as you go. You worry about it all the way home.
opt.right.say.1 [e5065b] = 你牵着一只瘦瘦的、黏糊糊的手，把他送到巡夜队的岗房，一个显然干过上百回这种事的警长让他坐在炉子边，给了块饼干。你走的时候他没看你。你一路回家都在担心。

@event streets_runaway_bride
# en: Drive, Anywhere
title [8582ca] = 走，去哪儿都行
# en: You've just hailed a cab when a young woman in a wedding dress comes running down the steps of a church across the road, her veil streaming, and jumps into it ahead of you. "Drive!" she tells the cabby. "Anywhere!" Then she looks at you, holding the door. "Well? Are you coming or not?"
text [eaa2b2] = 你刚叫住一辆出租马车，一个穿婚纱的年轻女人就从街对面教堂的台阶上跑下来，面纱飘着，抢在你前面跳上了车。“走！”她对车夫说，“去哪儿都行！”然后她看着扶着车门的你。“怎么样？你上不上来？”
# en: A city street, a young woman in a wedding dress and veil climbing into a hackney cab, a student holding the cab door, a church in the background with people running out of it.
scene [5535a0] = 城市街道，一个穿婚纱戴面纱的年轻女人爬进一辆出租马车，一个学生扶着车门，背景里的教堂里有人跑出来。
# en: Give her the cab, and walk
opt.left.label [b161bc] = 把车让给她，自己走
# en: You shut the door on her and slap the cab's side, and it rattles off with the veil streaming out of the window like a flag. Behind you a groom's party comes running down the steps and stops, defeated, beside you. It's a long walk home.
opt.left.say.1 [885d84] = 你替她关上门，拍了拍车厢，马车哐啷驶去，面纱像旗子一样从窗口飘出来。你身后，新郎那帮人跑下台阶，在你旁边垂头丧气地停住。回家的路很长。
# en: Ride along and hear her out
opt.right.label [4f6b0e] = 陪她坐一程，听她说
# en: You split the fare to the coaching yard. On the way she tells you everything: a match her father made with a man of fifty and a brewery, and a ticket north she's had sewn in her hem for a month. You wave her off on the night coach, with your purse lighter.
opt.right.say.1 [d3dca8] = 你们平摊了去驿车场的车费。路上她把一切都告诉了你：她父亲给她定了一门亲事，对方五十岁，有一家啤酒厂；还有一张往北的车票，她缝在裙摆里已经一个月了。你挥手送她上了夜班马车，钱袋轻了些。

@event streets_pieman
# en: The Pieman's Toss
title [209973] = 卖馅饼的抛硬币
# en: The pieman's tray of hot pies smells of pepper and gravy, and he has a game: he'll toss you for it. Call it right and the pie's free. Call it wrong and you pay double. "Fair as the King's justice," he says, flipping the coin, "and twice as quick."
text [3f2ac0] = 卖馅饼的托盘上热馅饼飘着胡椒和肉汁的香味，他有个玩法：跟你抛硬币赌。猜对了馅饼白送。猜错了付双倍。“公平得像国王的审判，”他抛着硬币说，“还快两倍。”
# en: A city street, a pieman with a tray of hot pies on his head and a coin spinning in the air above his hand, a laughing crowd, a student calling it.
scene [6eee83] = 城市街道，一个头顶热馅饼托盘的小贩，手上方一枚硬币在空中旋转，人群哄笑，一个学生在猜正反。
# en: Toss him for it
opt.left.label [4a3264] = 跟他抛硬币赌
# en: Double the price goes on his tray first.
opt.left.hint [0028f1] = 先把双倍的价钱放在他的托盘上。
# en: Heads, you call, and heads it is. He hands back your coins and the pie with a groan for the crowd, and you eat it standing in the street, scalding your mouth, the finest pie you've ever eaten for nothing.
opt.left.say.1 [f7f525] = 你喊正面，果然是正面。他冲人群哀叹一声，把你的钱和馅饼一起递还给你，你站在街上吃，烫了嘴，这是你白吃过的最好吃的馅饼。
# en: Tails. He sweeps the double price off his tray into his apron, and bows to the crowd. The pie's good, which almost makes up for it. Almost.
opt.left.say.2 [3524fc] = 反面。他把托盘上的双倍价钱一把扫进围裙，向人群鞠躬。馅饼不错，差不多能弥补。差不多。
# en: Watch the others call it
opt.right.label [e3f907] = 看别人猜
# en: You stand and watch the next dozen tosses, and see it: he calls the coin while it's still in the air and catches it the way he likes. You walk on hungry, with the smell of pepper and gravy following you down the street.
opt.right.say.1 [4a9845] = 你站着看了接下来的十几次，看出了门道：硬币还在空中他就喊了，然后照他想要的那面接住。你饿着肚子走了，胡椒和肉汁的香味一路跟着你。

@event streets_paint_pot
# en: Green Paint
title [1fe558] = 绿油漆
# en: A painter on the scaffolding outside a bank fumbles his pot. It turns over once in the air, very slowly, full of bright green paint, straight above a lady in an enormous hat.
text [8c65b0] = 银行外脚手架上的油漆工失手掉了漆桶。它在空中慢慢翻了一个身，满满一桶亮绿色的油漆，正对着下面一位戴着巨大帽子的女士。
# en: A city street, a house painter on high scaffolding fumbling a pot of bright green paint, the pot tipping, a lady in a large hat walking below, a student reaching up.
scene [de65cb] = 城市街道，一个油漆工在高高的脚手架上失手，一桶亮绿色的油漆翻倒下来，一位戴大帽子的女士在下面走，一个学生伸手去接。
# en: Catch the pot
opt.left.label [78424c] = 接住漆桶
# en: You step in and take it out of the air in both hands, upright, with hardly a splash. The lady never knows. The painter comes down the ladder to shake your green hand, and the street, which saw, gives you a round.
opt.left.say.1 [4db9e9] = 你一步上前，双手从空中稳稳接住，桶口朝上，几乎没溅出来。那位女士始终不知道。油漆工从梯子上下来握你那只绿手，看见了这一幕的整条街为你鼓掌。
# en: You get your fingers to it and turn it over again, and it empties itself down your front, collar to boots. The lady walks on, unspotted, quite unaware. People stare at you all the way home.
opt.left.say.2 [87cf10] = 你的手指碰到了它，却又把它翻了过去，油漆从你领口一路泼到靴子。那位女士毫发无污地走了，浑然不知。你一路回家都有人盯着你看。
# en: Shout a warning
opt.right.label [79e439] = 大喊提醒
# en: You shout, and she looks up and steps back, and the pot bursts on the pavement where she'd have been. The painter's whole morning of paint is in the gutter, and he swears at you from the scaffolding as if it were all your fault.
opt.right.say.1 [8f0844] = 你一喊，她抬头往后一退，漆桶砸在她刚才站的人行道上炸开。油漆工一上午的漆全进了水沟，他从脚手架上冲你破口大骂，好像全是你的错。

@event streets_fountain
# en: The Heatwave
title [b905df] = 热浪
# en: It's the hottest day anyone remembers, and the city has given up. In the square the big fountain is full of people paddling: clerks with their trousers rolled, shop girls holding their skirts, an alderman in his hat. The watchman on the corner is studiously looking the other way.
text [f106c2] = 这是人们记忆里最热的一天，整座城都放弃了。广场上的大喷泉里满是蹚水的人：卷着裤腿的书记员，提着裙子的店员姑娘，戴着帽子的市议员。街角的巡夜人刻意地看着别处。
# en: A city square in a summer heatwave, clerks and shop girls with their shoes off paddling in a big public fountain, a watchman pretending not to see, a student sitting on the rim.
scene [8ae264] = 夏日热浪中的城市广场，脱了鞋的书记员和店员姑娘在一座大公共喷泉里蹚水，一个巡夜人假装没看见，一个学生坐在池沿上。
# en: Take your shoes off and paddle
opt.left.label [3adf0f] = 脱了鞋去蹚水
# en: You sit on the rim and put your feet in, and the cold goes all the way up. Then a sketch artist from Printing Row draws the whole fountain for tomorrow's broadsheet, and you're in it, quite recognisably, with your trousers rolled to the knee.
opt.left.say.1 [81c0ff] = 你坐在池沿上把脚伸进去，凉意一路往上窜。然后一个印刷街的速写画家为明天的大字报画下了整座喷泉，你也在里面，一眼就认得出，裤腿卷到膝盖。
# en: Find a cool church porch
opt.right.label [51a0c7] = 找个凉快的教堂门廊
# en: You sit out the heat in the porch of an old church, where the stone is cold, and read the memorial tablets on the walls: merchants, sea captains, a famous dog. It's cool, and quiet, and you can hear the fun in the square the whole time.
opt.right.say.1 [37d5f4] = 你在一座老教堂的门廊里躲过酷热，石头是凉的，你读着墙上的纪念碑文：商人、船长、一条有名的狗。这里凉快、安静，而你一直听得见广场上的热闹。

@event streets_chess_hustler
# en: Three Boards at Once
title [ae9c56] = 一人三盘
# en: An old man with a folding table is playing three games of chess at once on the pavement, a coin a game, five to one to anyone who beats him, and winning all three while eating a sausage. There's a fourth board, empty. "Sit," he says, without looking up. "You've a face for losing."
text [e729a3] = 一个老头支着折叠桌在人行道上同时下三盘棋，一枚硬币一局，谁赢了他赔五倍，他一边吃香肠一边三盘全赢。还有第四张棋盘，空着。“坐，”他头也不抬地说，“你长了张输棋的脸。”
# en: A city pavement, an old man at a folding table playing three chess games at once against three challengers, a tin of coins beside him, a student sitting down at the empty fourth board.
scene [0a464c] = 城市人行道上，一个老头在折叠桌边同时和三个挑战者下三盘棋，身边放着一罐硬币，一个学生在空着的第四张棋盘前坐下。
# en: Play him for a coin
opt.left.label [c70096] = 跟他下一局赌一枚硬币
# en: A coin in his tin to sit down.
opt.left.hint [55c072] = 往他罐子里放一枚硬币才能坐下。
# en: You play slow and careful, and he plays fast and careless, and on the fortieth move he looks at the board for the first time and laughs and tips his king. "Come back when you're good," he says, paying you five to one, "and I'll take it all back."
opt.left.say.1 [3ecac3] = 你下得慢而谨慎，他下得快而随意，到第四十步他第一次正眼看棋盘，笑着推倒了他的王。“等你下好了再来，”他一边按五赔一付钱一边说，“我会全赢回来。”
# en: He mates you in eleven moves without breaking off his sausage. Your coin stays in his tin. He tells you what you did wrong, in detail, and he's right about all of it.
opt.left.say.2 [9ffc85] = 他十一步就将死了你，香肠都没停下。你的硬币留在了他的罐子里。他详详细细地告诉你哪里下错了，每一条都对。
# en: Watch and learn his trick
opt.right.label [d44c38] = 在旁边看，学他的招
# en: You stand behind him through six games and see it: he lets every opponent take the same pawn, and they all do. After the sixth he turns round and glares at you until you go away, feeling as if you'd stolen something.
opt.right.say.1 [b56ef3] = 你在他身后站了六局，看出来了：他让每个对手吃同一个兵，他们个个都吃。第六局后他转过身瞪着你，直到你走开，觉得自己好像偷了什么东西。

@event streets_rag_and_bone
# en: The Rag-and-Bone Cart
title [92faab] = 收破烂的车
# en: The rag-and-bone man's cart comes down the lane, piled with broken chairs, old boots and a birdcage, and in a box on top, among the rags, a set of old spellbooks, water-stained, the real thing. "House clearance," he says. "Some old wizard's. Penny a pound."
text [0666ef] = 收破烂的车沿着小巷过来，堆着破椅子、旧靴子和一个鸟笼，最上面一个箱子里，破布中间，放着一套旧法术书，有水渍，是真东西。“清房子收来的，”他说，“哪个老巫师的。一便士一磅。”
# en: A rag-and-bone man's cart in a city lane piled with junk, a tired pony, a box of water-stained old spellbooks among the rags, a student lifting one out.
scene [35ee8c] = 城市小巷里一辆堆满杂物的收破烂马车，一匹疲惫的小马，破布中间一箱有水渍的旧法术书，一个学生拿起了其中一本。
# en: Buy the box
opt.left.label [094919] = 买下那一箱
# en: You pay by the pound and carry the box home in your arms. The books are a dead wizard's working copies, crammed with notes in the margins, half of them corrections to the text and some of them very rude. It cost more than you meant to spend.
opt.left.say.1 [509779] = 你按磅付钱，把箱子抱回家。这些书是一位过世巫师的工作用本，页边写满了笔记，一半是对正文的更正，有些相当粗鲁。花的钱比你打算的多。
# en: Tell him what they're worth
opt.right.label [a79760] = 告诉他这些书值多少
# en: You tell him the truth: take them to the book stalls at the bazaar and they'll pay twenty times his price. He looks at you a long while, then at the books, and drives off to the bazaar without selling you so much as a page.
opt.right.say.1 [d28987] = 你告诉他实话：拿到大集市的书摊去，人家会出他要价的二十倍。他看了你好一会儿，又看看那些书，赶着车往大集市去了，一页也没卖给你。

@event streets_mistaken
# en: You're the One
title [5d2427] = 就是你
# en: A woman with a parasol seizes your arm in the middle of the street. "It's you!" she says. "From the play! At the theatre! You were wonderful, you were the villain!" She is quite sure. Passers-by are turning to see who you are.
text [e99131] = 一个打着阳伞的女人在街中间一把抓住你的胳膊。“是你！”她说，“演戏的那个！在剧院！你演得太好了，你演的是反派！”她十分确定。路人纷纷转过头来看你是谁。
# en: A busy city street, an excited woman with a parasol clutching a student's arm and talking at them, passers-by turning to look.
scene [2cec0a] = 繁忙的城市街道，一个兴奋的打阳伞的女人抓着一个学生的胳膊滔滔不绝，路人转头张望。
# en: Play along
opt.left.label [55ddb6] = 顺着她演
# en: You were the villain, you agree, and you tell her how the trapdoor works, and how the leading lady is in private, and she buys you tea and cake and makes you sign her programme. It's the best tea you've had in weeks, and every crumb of it a lie.
opt.left.say.1 [098e17] = 你承认你就是那个反派，还告诉她活板门是怎么用的，女主角私底下是什么样，她请你喝茶吃蛋糕，还让你在她的节目单上签名。这是你几个星期来喝过最好的茶，每一口都是谎话。
# en: You get halfway through the trapdoor before she says, "But the villain was a man of sixty," and lets go of your arm, and tells the whole street what you are, at length.
opt.left.say.2 [8de424] = 你才讲到活板门一半，她就说：“可演反派的是个六十岁的男人。”然后松开你的胳膊，向整条街长篇大论地宣布你是个什么东西。
# en: Tell her the truth
opt.right.label [bfb1ef] = 告诉她实话
# en: You tell her, gently, that you've never been in that play, and were nobody's villain. She doesn't believe you. She thinks you're being modest. She walks off telling her friend she met the villain and the villain was very modest, and you're left a little sorry not to be.
opt.right.say.1 [ffd07e] = 你温和地告诉她，你从没演过那出戏，也不是谁的反派。她不信。她觉得你在谦虚。她走开时对朋友说她见到了那个反派，反派非常谦虚，留下你有点遗憾自己不是。

@event streets_soup_kitchen
# en: Soup Under the Arch
title [822af5] = 拱门下的汤
# en: Under an arch by the river there's a soup kitchen that opens when the night does: a copper pot as big as a bath, steam going up in the lamplight, a queue of night-workers, watchmen and people with nowhere else. The woman ladling has been at it since six and drops the ladle when she sees you. "Hands," she says. "Thank the Lamp."
text [274b2d] = 河边一座拱门下有个施汤处，夜一来就开张：一口澡盆那么大的铜锅，蒸汽在灯光里往上冒，排队的有夜班工人、巡夜人，还有无处可去的人。掌勺的女人从六点忙到现在，一见你就把勺子掉了。“来帮手了，”她说，“感谢明灯。”
# en: A soup kitchen at night under a stone arch by the river, a great steaming copper pot, night-workers and the poor queuing with bowls, a student ladling soup.
scene [e56a1d] = 夜里河边石拱门下的施汤处，一口冒着热气的大铜锅，夜班工人和穷人端着碗排队，一个学生在盛汤。
# en: Take the ladle for an hour
opt.left.label [68ff43] = 接过勺子干一个钟头
# en: You ladle for an hour, and then another, and learn the queue's names and who's to have extra. By the end your wrist aches and your clothes smell of onions. The woman makes you eat the last bowl yourself, standing up.
opt.left.say.1 [c0a4bf] = 你盛了一个钟头，又一个钟头，记住了排队人的名字，知道谁该多给一勺。最后你手腕酸疼，衣服一股洋葱味。那女人让你站着把最后一碗喝了。
# en: Eat with the night-workers
opt.right.label [7595bc] = 和夜班工人一起喝汤
# en: You put a coin in the box and take a bowl and sit with the lamplighters and a night-watchman on an upturned crate. They tell you the city by night: who's out, what's open, which bridge to keep off. It's the best soup in the capital.
opt.right.say.1 [8bc2a6] = 你往箱子里放了一枚硬币，端了一碗，和几个点灯人、一个巡夜人坐在一只倒扣的板条箱上。他们给你讲夜里的城：谁在外面，什么还开着，哪座桥别去。这是首都最好喝的汤。

@event streets_top_hat
# en: The Runaway Hat
title [b460da] = 逃跑的礼帽
# en: A gust comes up the street off the river and takes a gentleman's top hat clean off his head. It bowls away down the cobbles on its brim like a hoop, faster than he can run, towards the embankment and the water.
text [c5a69a] = 一阵风从河上沿街刮来，把一位绅士的高礼帽从头上掀了下来。它帽檐着地，像个铁环一样沿着石子路滚走，比他跑得还快，直奔河堤和河水。
# en: A windy city street, a tall black top hat bowling along the cobbles towards the river, a portly gentleman running after it, a student giving chase.
scene [7fd2cb] = 刮风的城市街道，一顶黑色高礼帽沿着石子路往河边滚，一位胖绅士在后面追，一个学生也追了上去。
# en: Run it down
opt.left.label [69bc99] = 追上它
# en: You catch it at the very last bollard, on your knees, an inch from the river. The gentleman arrives purple and wheezing and gives you a coin, and then brushes the hat very carefully and puts it back on, and the wind takes it again. You leave him to it, nursing a skinned knee.
opt.left.say.1 [50f8b8] = 你在最后一根系船柱边跪着接住了它，离河只差一寸。绅士赶来，脸涨得发紫、喘个不停，给了你一枚硬币，然后非常仔细地掸掸帽子戴上，风又把它刮走了。你让他自己去追，揉着蹭破的膝盖。
# en: Call it back with a spell
opt.right.label [e707ca] = 用法术把它叫回来
# en: You hook a finger, and the hat stops, turns round on its brim and bowls back up the street to its owner, who catches it, stares at it and at you, and lifts it to you very formally before he puts it on.
opt.right.say.1 [abde9d] = 你勾了勾手指，礼帽停住，在帽檐上转了个身，沿街滚回主人那里，他接住它，盯着它又盯着你，然后非常郑重地向你举了举帽子，才戴上。
# en: Your spell catches the hat and lifts it, beautifully, over the embankment wall, and drops it in the river. It sails away towards the sea upright. The gentleman watches it go and then looks at you for a long, long time.
opt.right.say.2 [4e2791] = 你的法术兜住了礼帽，把它漂亮地举过河堤墙，然后扔进了河里。它端端正正地朝大海漂走了。绅士看着它远去，然后看了你很久很久。

@event streets_shoeblack
# en: The Shoeblack
title [17c4ce] = 擦鞋童
# en: A shoeblack on the corner, a lanky young man all elbows and cheek, offers to black your boots and tell you the street's news, both for one coin. His own boots, you notice, are grey with dust and have never seen a brush in their lives.
text [d6b817] = 街角一个擦鞋的瘦高小伙子，满身胳膊肘和机灵劲儿，提出一枚硬币给你擦靴子，再附送街上的新闻。你注意到他自己的靴子灰扑扑的，这辈子从没见过刷子。
# en: A city street corner, a lanky young shoeblack with his box and brushes sitting on it while a student kneels to black his own worn boots, passers-by amused.
scene [681581] = 城市街角，一个瘦高的年轻擦鞋匠坐在自己的鞋箱上，一个学生跪着给他擦那双旧靴子，路人看得发笑。
# en: Pay for the shine and the news
opt.left.label [20d2e7] = 付钱擦鞋听新闻
# en: He blacks your boots till you can see your face in them and tells you the street as he goes: who owes who, whose shop is going under, which watchman takes a pie on Fridays. You walk away shining and much better informed, a coin lighter.
opt.left.say.1 [e32750] = 他把你的靴子擦得能照出人脸，一边擦一边讲这条街：谁欠谁的钱，谁家的店要倒，哪个巡夜人每星期五收一个馅饼。你走的时候靴子锃亮，消息灵通多了，少了一枚硬币。
# en: Black his boots instead
opt.right.label [fc244f] = 反过来给他擦
# en: You sit him on his own box and kneel on the cobbles and black his boots, while the street stops to laugh. He sits like a duke the whole time, very straight. When you stand up your knees are aching and your hands are black, and he's grinning from ear to ear.
opt.right.say.1 [0cf836] = 你让他坐在自己的鞋箱上，你跪在石子路上给他擦靴子，整条街都停下来笑。他一直坐得笔挺，像个公爵。你站起来时膝盖酸疼，手也黑了，他笑得合不拢嘴。

@event streets_knife_thrower
# en: A Volunteer, Please
title [0c5514] = 请一位志愿者
# en: A knife-thrower in spangles is working the square, and his assistant hasn't turned up. He needs a volunteer for the board, the one with the painted outline, and he's looking straight at your scarf. "A wizard," he tells the crowd. "If I miss, they can fix it."
text [af4a3e] = 一个穿亮片衣服的飞刀手在广场上表演，他的助手没来。他需要一位志愿者站到那块画着人形轮廓的木板前，眼睛直直地盯着你的围巾。“一位巫师，”他对人群说，“要是我失手了，他们能治好。”
# en: A street performance in a city square, a knife-thrower in spangles holding three knives, a painted wooden board with an outline of a person on it, a crowd, a student stepping forward.
scene [794765] = 城市广场上的街头表演，一个穿亮片衣服的飞刀手握着三把刀，一块画着人形轮廓的木板，一圈观众，一个学生走上前。
# en: Stand at the board
opt.left.label [77a1c3] = 站到木板前
# en: You stand against the board and he throws: left ear, right ear, between your knees, and one an inch over your head. The crowd goes wild. You walk away to a great deal of applause, with your legs not quite working and your heart going like a drum.
opt.left.say.1 [e696af] = 你靠着木板站好，他扔了：左耳边、右耳边、两膝之间，还有一把离你头顶一寸。人群疯了。你在一片掌声中走开，腿不太听使唤，心跳得像擂鼓。
# en: Pass the hat for him instead
opt.right.label [bf7b89] = 改为替他收钱
# en: You beg off the board and take the hat round instead, and he gives you a cut. The square is mean with its coins and a man in a good coat tells you to get a proper job. A young woman from the crowd stands at the board and is far braver than you.
opt.right.say.1 [39f687] = 你推掉了木板，改为端着帽子绕场收钱，他分你一份。广场上的人很抠，一个穿好外套的男人叫你去找份正经工作。人群里一个年轻女人站到了木板前，比你勇敢多了。

@event streets_crooked_scales
# en: A Thumb on the Scale
title [0014ac] = 秤上的拇指
# en: At a market stall a trader is weighing tea for an old woman, and smiling, and his thumb is resting very lightly on the pan. She's counting out coppers she can't spare for a quarter she isn't getting. Nobody else in the queue has noticed.
text [96ca29] = 一个集市摊位上，摊主正给一位老妇人称茶叶，脸上带笑，拇指轻轻搭在秤盘上。她数着自己舍不得的铜板，买的是她拿不到的四分之一磅。队伍里没别人注意到。
# en: A city market stall, a smiling trader weighing tea on brass scales with his thumb resting on the pan, an old woman counting coins, a student watching closely.
scene [39a51a] = 城市集市摊位，一个笑眯眯的摊主用黄铜秤称茶叶，拇指搭在秤盘上，一位老妇人在数硬币，一个学生在一旁仔细看着。
# en: Lean on the other pan
opt.left.label [18cce0] = 按住另一只秤盘
# en: You lean on the counter, chatting, with one finger resting on the other pan, just as light as his. The scales come level. He can't say a word without saying why. The old woman gets her full quarter, and he watches you go with murder in his eyes.
opt.left.say.1 [1035b6] = 你靠在柜台上闲聊，一根手指搭在另一只秤盘上，和他的一样轻。秤平了。他一个字也说不出，除非说出为什么。老妇人拿到了足足四分之一磅，他看着你离开，眼里杀气腾腾。
# en: He sees your finger, and shouts "Cheat!" at the top of his voice, and the whole queue turns on you. You leave fast, red to the ears, and the old woman still pays for her short quarter.
opt.left.say.2 [4fcb85] = 他看见了你的手指，扯着嗓子大喊“骗子！”，整条队伍都冲你来了。你赶紧溜走，耳朵通红，老妇人还是为她缺斤短两的茶叶付了钱。
# en: Quietly make up her difference
opt.right.label [2c95eb] = 悄悄替她补上差额
# en: You catch her at the end of the street and press a coin into her hand for the missing ounce, saying she dropped it. She looks at you sharply and doesn't believe a word, and takes it anyway. The trader goes on smiling.
opt.right.say.1 [978a07] = 你在街尾追上她，往她手里塞了一枚硬币补那缺的一盎司，说是她掉的。她锐利地看了你一眼，一个字也不信，但还是收下了。摊主照旧笑着。

@event streets_sleeping_cabby
# en: The Horse Knows the Way
title [6e91f1] = 马认得路
# en: Late at night, under a lamp, there's a hackney cab waiting with its cabby fast asleep on the box, snoring, his whip in his lap. The old horse looks round at you with great patience. It seems to be asking whether you're going its way.
text [800d55] = 深夜，一盏路灯下停着一辆出租马车，车夫在驾座上睡得正香，打着呼，鞭子搁在腿上。老马极有耐心地回头看你，好像在问你是不是顺路。
# en: A city street late at night, a hackney cab under a gas lamp with its cabby fast asleep on the box, the old horse patiently waiting, a student looking up at the cabby.
scene [777b12] = 深夜的城市街道，煤气灯下一辆出租马车，车夫在驾座上熟睡，老马耐心地等着，一个学生抬头看着车夫。
# en: Wake him and take the cab home
opt.left.label [65e51f] = 叫醒他，坐车回家
# en: You shake his boot, and he wakes, embarrassed, and takes you home at a stately walk, apologising the whole way. You fall into bed with your feet still fresh, a coin poorer.
opt.left.say.1 [bd385e] = 你摇了摇他的靴子，他醒了，很不好意思，以庄重的步速送你回家，一路道歉。你倒在床上时脚还很轻松，少了一枚硬币。
# en: Climb up and let the horse drive
opt.right.label [225df1] = 爬上去让马自己走
# en: You climb up beside the sleeping cabby and say "Home," to the horse, and it walks off through the empty streets on its own, the long way, past the river and the dark markets, and stops at its own stable. The cabby never wakes. You walk the rest of the way back, chilled.
opt.right.say.1 [68e651] = 你爬到熟睡的车夫身边，对马说了声“回家”，它就自己穿过空荡荡的街道走了，绕了远路，经过河边和黑沉沉的市场，停在它自己的马厩前。车夫始终没醒。你走完剩下的路回去，冻得发抖。

@event streets_muffin_men
# en: The Muffin Men
title [15a681] = 卖松饼的
# en: Two muffin men have met in the same street, one on each pavement, trays on their heads, and neither will give way. They're out-shouting each other: "Hot muffins!" "Hotter muffins!" The street has stopped to watch. Then both of them point at you. "You," they say. "Judge."
text [04a7e3] = 两个卖松饼的在同一条街碰上了，一人一边人行道，头顶托盘，谁也不让。他们比着吆喝：“热松饼！”“更热的松饼！”整条街都停下来看。然后两人一起指着你。“你，”他们说，“来评评。”
# en: A winter city street, two muffin men with trays on their heads, shouting at each other from opposite pavements, a laughing crowd, a student caught in the middle.
scene [f03930] = 冬天的城市街道，两个头顶托盘的卖松饼小贩隔着人行道对喊，人群哄笑，一个学生被夹在中间。
# en: Judge for one of them
opt.left.label [9a9abe] = 评其中一个赢
# en: You taste one of each, very gravely, and give it to the one on the left, whose muffin is better and whose shouting is worse. The street cheers. The one on the right tells you exactly what he thinks of academies, all the way down the street.
opt.left.say.1 [500806] = 你一本正经地各尝了一个，判左边那个赢，他的松饼更好，吆喝更差。整条街欢呼。右边那个一路沿街告诉你他对学院到底怎么看。
# en: Buy from both and refuse to choose
opt.right.label [3966e5] = 两家都买，拒绝评判
# en: You buy a muffin from each of them and eat them both, one in each hand, and declare it a draw. Both are disgusted with you. They go off down the street together, complaining about you, and by the corner they're friends.
opt.right.say.1 [b1eb07] = 你从两人手里各买了一个，一手一个吃光，宣布平局。两人都对你嗤之以鼻。他们一起沿街走了，一路抱怨你，到街角时已经成了朋友。

@event lanes_strawberries
# en: Wild Strawberries
title [69887e] = 野草莓
# en: The bank under the hedge is warm with sun, and when you look down it's red with wild strawberries, tiny ones, hidden among the grass and the nettles, sweeter than any in a shop. Across the field, the haymakers are working on through the heat.
text [0fae6a] = 树篱下的土坡被太阳晒得暖暖的，低头一看，满坡红红的野草莓，小小的，藏在草丛和荨麻里，比店里卖的任何草莓都甜。田那头，割草的人还顶着暑热干活。
# en: A sunny bank under a country hedge, tiny wild strawberries hidden in the grass, a student kneeling and picking them into a hat.
scene [71cb67] = 乡间树篱下一片向阳的土坡，小小的野草莓藏在草丛里，一个学生跪着把草莓摘进帽子里。
# en: Pick and eat them where you are
opt.left.label [5b825d] = 就地摘了吃
# en: You lie on the bank and eat them one by one as you find them, warm from the sun, till your fingers are red and you can't find any more. The nettles have got both your wrists.
opt.left.say.1 [a5c79e] = 你躺在坡上，找到一颗吃一颗，个个带着太阳的温度，直到手指染红、再也找不到了。荨麻把你两只手腕都蜇了。
# en: Fill your hat for the haymakers
opt.right.label [45f76d] = 摘满一帽子给晒草的人
# en: You fill your hat, carefully, without eating more than one in five, and carry it to the field gate, where three hot haymakers fall on it like starlings. You've been stung from your knuckles to your elbows.
opt.right.say.1 [0a3d3c] = 你小心地摘满一帽子，五颗里最多吃一颗，捧到田边的门口，三个热得冒汗的晒草人像椋鸟一样扑了上来。你从指关节到胳膊肘都被蜇遍了。

@event lanes_shearing
# en: The Shearers
title [998b7f] = 剪羊毛的人
# en: The shearers have come to a farm by the lane, and the yard is all bleating and wool. The champion of the valley is taking a fleece off in one piece, quick as peeling an orange. He holds the shears out to you, grinning. "Your go," he says. "Mind her, she's got opinions."
text [a6d7e4] = 剪羊毛的人来到小路边的一座农场，院子里全是咩咩声和羊毛。山谷的冠军正把一整张羊毛剪下来，快得像剥橘子。他咧嘴笑着把剪子递给你。“该你了，”他说，“当心，她可有主见。”
# en: A farmyard in summer, sheep being shorn in the shade of a barn, a champion shearer with a fleece coming off in one piece, wool everywhere, a student holding a pair of shears.
scene [3ff46e] = 夏天的农家院子，谷仓阴凉处正在剪羊毛，一位冠军剪毛手剪下一整张羊毛，到处都是羊毛，一个学生拿着一把剪子。
# en: Shear a ewe
opt.left.label [824716] = 剪一只母羊
# en: It takes you four times as long as him, and the fleece comes off in three pieces, but it comes off, and the ewe trots away looking quite pleased with herself. The yard applauds. The champion says you've the makings, with practice. Thirty years of it.
opt.left.say.1 [4b5b0c] = 你花的时间是他的四倍，羊毛分成了三块，但总算剪下来了，母羊一溜小跑地走开，看上去对自己挺满意。院子里一片掌声。冠军说你有这块料，练练就行。练上三十年。
# en: The ewe has her opinions, all of them, and you end up underneath her in the straw with the shears somewhere else. The yard laughs till it cries. The champion takes her off you and finishes in a minute flat. You're bruised all down one side.
opt.left.say.2 [f330be] = 母羊把它所有的主见都亮了出来，你最后被它压在稻草里，剪子不知飞到了哪儿。院子里的人笑出了眼泪。冠军把它从你身上弄下来，一分钟就剪完了。你半边身子都是淤青。
# en: Roll fleeces for them
opt.right.label [49a182] = 帮他们卷羊毛
# en: You spend the afternoon rolling fleeces and stuffing them into the long wool sacks, greasy to the elbows with lanolin. Your hands are softer than they've ever been, and your back is killing you.
opt.right.say.1 [9fbd12] = 你花了一下午卷羊毛，塞进长长的羊毛袋，羊毛脂一直糊到胳膊肘。你的手从没这么软过，腰却快断了。

@event lanes_cricket
# en: Was It Out?
title [bd138c] = 出局了吗？
# en: The two villages are playing their annual match on the green, and it comes down to the last ball: a catch, or a bounce, nobody's sure. The umpire is the miller's brother, so he won't do. {at_home(): Both captains turn and look at you: away at the academy so long, you hardly count as anybody's.|Both captains turn and look at the one person on the green with no side.}
text [17cc7a] = 两个村子在绿地上打一年一度的板球赛，胜负落在最后一球：是接杀，还是落地反弹，没人说得准。裁判是磨坊主的弟弟，所以不行。{at_home(): 两位队长转过来看着你：你在学院待了那么久，几乎算不上哪边的人了。|两位队长转过来，看着绿地上唯一不站任何一边的人。}
# en: A village cricket match on a green in summer, two teams in white arguing round a fielder holding up a ball, both captains turning to a student standing at the boundary rope.
scene [05b3dc] = 夏天绿地上的乡村板球赛，两队穿白衣的人围着一个举着球的外野手争吵，两位队长转向站在边界绳旁的一个学生。
# en: Rule it a catch
opt.left.label [c9da24] = 判接杀
# en: You say it was a catch. Half the green carries you round on its shoulders and the other half won't speak to you, and at the inn the visiting side drinks in the far corner with its back to you, very pointedly, all evening.
opt.left.say.1 [929596] = 你说是接杀。半个绿地把你扛上肩头绕场，另一半不跟你说话，到了客栈，客队一整晚都坐在最远的角落里，背对着你，非常刻意。
# en: Say you couldn't see
opt.right.label [63f9d0] = 说你没看清
# en: You say, truthfully, you were watching a swallow. Both captains are disgusted with you, and they argue it out themselves for an hour while you listen, and you learn the whole history of the two villages' feud, back to a stolen pig.
opt.right.say.1 [69fdab] = 你如实说，你当时在看一只燕子。两位队长都对你嗤之以鼻，他们自己吵了一个钟头，你在旁边听，听完了两个村子世仇的全部来历，一直追溯到一头被偷的猪。

@event lanes_glow_worms
# en: Glow-Worms
title [5a19b5] = 萤火虫
# en: The lane's verges are lit up in the dark: dozens of tiny cold green lights in the grass, steady and still, like somebody has scattered embers that don't burn. Glow-worms. You didn't know there were so many in the world.
text [232a97] = 小路两边的草地在黑暗里亮了起来：草丛里几十点冷冷的绿光，稳稳地一动不动，像有人撒了一地不烫的余烬。是萤火虫。你从不知道世上有这么多。
# en: A dark country lane on a warm summer night, dozens of tiny green glow-worm lights in the grass of the verges, a student kneeling to look closely.
scene [bc9c1d] = 温暖夏夜里一条黑暗的乡间小路，路边草丛里几十点绿色的萤光，一个学生跪下来凑近看。
# en: Lie in the verge and watch them
opt.left.label [ab2eea] = 躺在路边看它们
# en: You lie in the long grass at the edge of the lane with the green lights all round you, and lose track of time completely. When you get up the dew has soaked right through to your skin.
opt.left.say.1 [e68d47] = 你躺在小路边的长草里，周围全是绿光，完全忘了时间。站起来时，露水已经湿透到了皮肤。
# en: Catch one to look at closely
opt.right.label [13ddb6] = 捉一只来细看
# en: You cup one in your hand and look: a small, plain, wingless thing with its light in its tail. In your hand it goes dark at once. You put it back in the grass, and it takes a long while to light again, and you feel like a thief.
opt.right.say.1 [4c559d] = 你双手捧住一只细看：一只小小的、不起眼的、没有翅膀的虫子，光在尾巴上。在你手里它立刻暗了。你把它放回草丛，它过了好久才重新亮起，你觉得自己像个小偷。

@event lanes_thatcher
# en: The Thatcher
title [c6b9a1] = 铺茅草的人
# en: A thatcher is on the roof of a cottage by the lane, laying new straw over old. He sees you looking. "Come up and see," he calls down. "I'll show you how old this roof is, and you'll not believe me."
text [5c87d1] = 小路边一座小屋的屋顶上，一个铺茅草的人正把新草铺在旧草上。他看见你在看。“上来瞧瞧，”他朝下喊，“我让你看看这屋顶有多老，你准不信。”
# en: A thatcher working high on the roof of a country cottage, bundles of straw stacked against the wall, a student at the top of the ladder looking at the old layers of thatch.
scene [4c35c5] = 一个铺茅草的人在乡间小屋高高的屋顶上干活，一捆捆稻草靠墙堆着，一个学生站在梯子顶上看着一层层的旧茅草。
# en: Climb up and look
opt.left.label [f8088d] = 爬上去看看
# en: You go up the ladder and he lifts the top coat for you: under it the roof is four hundred years old, layer on layer, and the bottom straw is black as coal and full of old wasps' nests. Coming down, you miss a rung and graze your shins.
opt.left.say.1 [3ab738] = 你爬上梯子，他为你掀开最上面一层：下面的屋顶有四百年了，一层压一层，最底下的稻草黑得像煤，满是旧马蜂窝。下来时你踩空一级，蹭破了小腿。
# en: Stand him a drink for the story
opt.right.label [6a2c0d] = 请他喝一杯换个故事
# en: You buy him a jug of cider from the cottage, and he sits on the ridge drinking it and tells you about every roof in the valley: the oldest, the haunted one, the one with a gold coin in it for luck. You're a coin down and none the wiser about thatching.
opt.right.say.1 [a521e6] = 你从小屋里给他买了一壶苹果酒，他坐在屋脊上喝着，给你讲山谷里每一座屋顶：最老的、闹鬼的、里面藏着一枚金币保佑好运的。你少了一枚硬币，对铺茅草还是一窍不通。

@event lanes_bull
# en: The Bull in the Field
title [1fbfcf] = 田里的公牛
# en: The footpath crosses a meadow, the short way to where you're going. You're over the stile before you see the bull: huge and red, standing in the middle of the path, chewing slowly, looking at you. The far stile is a very long way off.
text [e84c6f] = 小径穿过一片草地，是去你要去的地方的近路。你翻过栅栏台阶才看见那头公牛：又大又红，站在小径正中，慢慢嚼着，看着你。对面的台阶远得很。
# en: A green meadow with a footpath across it, a huge red bull standing in the middle looking at a student who has just climbed over the stile, the far stile a long way off.
scene [bcba81] = 一片绿草地，一条小径横穿而过，一头巨大的红公牛站在中间看着一个刚翻过栅栏台阶的学生，对面的台阶远在另一头。
# en: Walk across, slow and calm
opt.left.label [c295f0] = 慢慢地、镇定地走过去
# en: You walk slowly, talking to him the whole way in a low, dull voice about nothing, and he watches you, chewing, and lets you by. At the far stile he blows through his nose at you, quite friendly. Your heart is going like a hammer.
opt.left.say.1 [905f28] = 你慢慢走，一路用低沉单调的声音对它说些没意思的话，它嚼着看你，让你过去了。到了对面台阶，它冲你喷了喷鼻子，挺友好。你的心跳得像锤子。
# en: Halfway across he lowers his head. You don't remember the rest of the field. You go over the far stile head first into a ditch full of water, and he stands at the stile, satisfied, and goes back to his grass.
opt.left.say.2 [bfe2dd] = 走到一半它低下了头。那片地剩下的部分你都不记得了。你头朝下翻过对面的台阶，栽进一条满是水的沟里，它站在台阶边，心满意足，回去吃它的草了。
# en: Go the long way round
opt.right.label [6afca9] = 绕远路
# en: You climb back over and take the long way round, two miles of lane, and find an old lime kiln in the hedge you'd never have seen, with a date carved over its arch. Your feet are sore by the time you get there.
opt.right.say.1 [3c91e2] = 你翻回去，绕了两英里的小路，在树篱里发现了一座你本来绝不会看见的旧石灰窑，拱门上刻着年份。到地方时你的脚已经疼了。

@event lanes_new_gate
# en: Private, By Order
title [7a9849] = 私人领地，奉命
# en: Across the old footpath, the one everybody uses, somebody has put up a new gate with a padlock and a fresh-painted sign: PRIVATE. BY ORDER. The path is worn into the grass on both sides of it, a hundred years deep.
text [32a51f] = 人人都走的那条老小径上，有人装了一扇新门，挂着挂锁和一块刚漆好的牌子：私人领地。奉命设立。门两边的草地上踩出的小路，有一百年那么深。
# en: A country footpath blocked by a brand new padlocked gate with a painted sign reading PRIVATE, an old path beaten into the grass on both sides of it, a student considering climbing it.
scene [38fd44] = 一条乡间小径被一扇崭新的上了挂锁的门拦住，门上漆着“私人领地”的牌子，门两边的草地上踩出一条老路，一个学生在考虑要不要翻过去。
# en: Climb over and walk on
opt.left.label [86c74f] = 翻过去接着走
# en: You climb over, which is what the path's for, and walk on. On the far side a whole row of village boots has gone over the gate before you: the top bar's already muddy. You graze your shin on the new wire.
opt.left.say.1 [b8ae4b] = 你翻了过去，这条路本来就是走的，接着往前。另一边，整整一排村里人的靴子已经在你之前翻过了这扇门：顶上的横杆早就沾满了泥。你的小腿被新铁丝刮破了。
# en: Take the sign to the village
opt.right.label [5087fc] = 把牌子带到村里去
# en: You unscrew the sign and carry it into the village and put it on the bar of the inn, and the whole taproom has an opinion about it, and a meeting is called, and you're made to stand on a chair and say where you found it. You're there half the evening.
opt.right.say.1 [e8c5cb] = 你拧下牌子，带进村里，放在客栈的吧台上，整个酒馆都对它有话说，于是召开了一场会，你被叫上椅子讲你是在哪儿找到它的。你在那儿耗了半个晚上。

@event lanes_poacher
# en: Not Seeing Things
title [bbc584] = 什么也没看见
# en: {slot == "night": In the dark|At dusk} a man comes through the hedge into the lane in front of you, thin, in a patched coat, with a sack over his shoulder and two pheasants' tails sticking out of the top. He stops dead. So do you. "I've five at home," he says, low. "And the keeper's up at the big house."
text [23368b] = {slot == "night": 黑暗中|黄昏时}，一个男人从树篱钻进你面前的小路，瘦瘦的，穿着打补丁的外套，肩上扛着一只口袋，口袋顶上露出两根野鸡尾巴。他猛地停住。你也是。“我家里有五个，”他低声说，“看林人在大宅那边。”
# en: A country lane at dusk, a thin poacher in a patched coat with a bulging sack over his shoulder, a pair of pheasants' tails sticking out, frozen in the hedge gap, a student facing him.
scene [3d557f] = 黄昏的乡间小路，一个穿补丁外套的瘦偷猎者肩扛鼓鼓的口袋，露出一对野鸡尾巴，僵在树篱缺口，一个学生面对着他。
# en: Keep his secret
opt.left.label [ef72f4] = 替他保守秘密
# en: You say you didn't see a thing. He nods, and then shows you, before he goes, where the keeper sets his traps along the hedges, so you'll know where not to walk. You go home not quite sure you did right.
opt.left.say.1 [a29218] = 你说你什么也没看见。他点点头，走之前告诉你看林人沿着树篱在哪儿下了套，好让你知道哪儿别走。你回家时，不太确定自己做得对不对。
# en: Turn him in at the big house
opt.right.label [99553d] = 去大宅告发他
# en: You go up to the big house and tell the keeper. There's a reward, a coin, and he pays it gladly. Walking home, you think about five children and two pheasants for a long time.
opt.right.say.1 [ffcc99] = 你上大宅去告诉了看林人。有赏钱，一枚硬币，他很乐意地付了。回家路上，你想了很久那五个孩子和两只野鸡。

@event lanes_sheepdog_trial
# en: The Dog Trial
title [53acae] = 牧羊犬比赛
# en: There's a dog trial on the hillside above the lane: one dog, three sheep, a course of gates and a little pen at the end, and the whole valley on the wall. Neither village will trust the other's man on the pen gate. "You," says the judge, picking {at_home(): the one face on the wall that's been away at school|the one stranger on the wall}. "Hold the gate rope. Shut it when they're in, and not before."
text [c32323] = 小路上方的山坡上在举行牧羊犬比赛：一条狗，三只羊，一串门，最后是一个小羊圈，全山谷的人都趴在墙上看。两个村子谁也不信对方的人守圈门。“你，”裁判说，挑中了{at_home(): 墙上唯一一个在外面上学的面孔|墙上唯一一个外乡人}。“拉着门绳。羊进去了再关，不能早。”
# en: A sheepdog trial on a summer hillside, a handler with a crook whistling, a black-and-white dog crouched behind three sheep, a small pen with a gate, a student holding the pen gate rope.
scene [e4fba6] = 夏天山坡上的牧羊犬比赛，一个拿着牧羊杖吹口哨的训犬人，一条黑白相间的狗伏在三只羊后面，一个带门的小羊圈，一个学生拉着圈门的绳子。
# en: Hold the pen gate
opt.left.label [c679a3] = 守住圈门
# en: The sheep come in at a run, the dog flat behind them, and you shut the gate on the last tail exactly as it clears. The wall roars. The handler shakes your hand as if you'd done it all, and the dog looks at you with something like respect.
opt.left.say.1 [3355d2] = 羊一路小跑进来，狗紧贴地面跟在后面，最后一条尾巴刚过你就关上了门，分秒不差。墙上一片欢呼。训犬人跟你握手，好像全是你的功劳，那条狗看你的眼神里有几分敬意。
# en: You shut it a heartbeat early and the last ewe turns and bolts, and the dog has to fetch her back from halfway up the hill. The handler loses on points. He doesn't say a word to you, which is worse.
opt.left.say.2 [8412d6] = 你早关了一瞬，最后一只母羊掉头就跑，狗只好从半山腰把它赶回来。训犬人输了分。他一句话也没对你说，这更糟。
# en: Sit on the wall and pick a winner
opt.right.label [601cb5] = 坐在墙上押一个赢家
# en: You sit on the wall among the farmers and put a coin on a grey-muzzled old dog everybody says is past it, and learn more about sheep than you meant to. It comes third. Your coin's gone, and you'd do it again.
opt.right.say.1 [60b3bc] = 你和农夫们一起坐在墙上，把一枚硬币押在一条人人都说老了的灰嘴老狗身上，学到的关于羊的事比你想学的还多。它得了第三。你的硬币没了，你还会再押。

@event lanes_hedger
# en: Laying the Hedge
title [7b0f2d] = 编树篱
# en: An old hedger in a leather apron is laying the hedge along the lane: cutting each stem nearly through with his billhook, bending it over, weaving it between stakes, so it grows again thick and sideways. He's been at it since dawn and is about a third of the way along.
text [dabbd1] = 一个系皮围裙的老树篱匠正在编小路边的树篱：用钩刀把每根枝干砍到快断，压弯，在木桩之间编起来，让它重新长得又密又横。他从天亮干起，大约编了三分之一。
# en: A winter country lane, an old hedger in a leather apron and gauntlets laying a hawthorn hedge with a billhook, the half-cut stems bent over and woven between stakes, a student watching.
scene [918377] = 冬天的乡间小路，一个系皮围裙戴护手的老树篱匠用钩刀编山楂树篱，砍了一半的枝干弯下来编在木桩之间，一个学生在一旁看着。
# en: Ask him to teach you the cut
opt.left.label [d8a034] = 请他教你砍法
# en: He shows you, patient as a stone, and lets you lay three stems. Two of them break. The third bends just right and he grunts, which is a great deal from him. The hawthorn has had its way with your hands.
opt.left.say.1 [3ead27] = 他像石头一样有耐心地教你，让你编了三根。两根断了。第三根弯得恰到好处，他哼了一声，这对他来说已经很多了。山楂刺把你的手扎了个遍。
# en: Share his tea at the fire
opt.right.label [e3c088] = 在火边和他喝茶
# en: You sit with him at his little brushwood fire on the verge while he drinks black tea out of a can, and he talks about the valley's hedges like old friends: which are a hundred years old and which are a thousand. Your feet go numb sitting there.
opt.right.say.1 [45bbad] = 你和他坐在路边一小堆柴火旁，他用罐子喝着浓茶，像谈老朋友一样谈山谷里的树篱：哪些有一百年，哪些有一千年。你坐得脚都麻了。

@event lanes_wassail
# en: Wassailing the Orchard
title [806fed] = 为果园祝酒
# en: In an orchard off the lane the farm is wassailing its trees: lanterns in the branches, a bonfire, everybody singing to the oldest apple tree to make it bear. Toast soaked in cider is hung in its branches for the robins. They need a guest to pour the cider on its roots, and you're the only guest there.
text [f89847] = 小路边的果园里，农场正在为果树祝酒：枝头挂着灯笼，燃着篝火，大家围着最老的那棵苹果树唱歌，盼它结果。泡了苹果酒的面包片挂在枝头给知更鸟。他们需要一位客人把苹果酒浇在树根上，而你是那里唯一的客人。
# en: A winter orchard at night lit by lanterns and a bonfire, villagers singing round the oldest apple tree, pieces of toast hung in its branches, cider poured on its roots, a student holding the wassail bowl.
scene [d0df39] = 冬夜的果园，灯笼和篝火照着，村民们围着最老的苹果树唱歌，枝头挂着面包片，苹果酒浇在树根上，一个学生捧着祝酒碗。
# en: Sing with them
opt.left.label [1cd794] = 和他们一起唱
# en: You sing every verse, badly, and drink from the bowl when it comes round, and bang a saucepan with a spoon at the end to wake the tree. By the time the bonfire's down your feet are numb with cold and you're very happy.
opt.left.say.1 [732628] = 你每一段都唱了，唱得很差，酒碗传到你手里就喝一口，最后拿勺子敲平底锅把树叫醒。等篝火烧尽，你的脚已经冻麻了，你非常快乐。
# en: Pour the cider on the roots
opt.right.label [a9a79e] = 把苹果酒浇在树根上
# en: You pour the bowl over the old tree's roots while the whole orchard sings to you, and the farmer's wife hangs the last of the toast. You're splashed to the knees, and the cold gets into you through the wet. Everybody tells you the tree will bear like never before.
opt.right.say.1 [a5be65] = 整个果园都在为你唱歌时，你把一碗酒浇在老树的根上，农夫的妻子挂上最后几片面包。酒溅到了你的膝盖，寒气顺着湿处钻进来。每个人都说这棵树会结得前所未有地好。

@event lanes_mummers
# en: The Mummers
title [70f7f4] = 哑剧艺人
# en: The mummers have come round to the farm by the lane in their costumes of paper strips: a knight, a dragon, a king, and a man with a sword who keeps killing everybody. By custom the Doctor is always somebody from the crowd. A mummer holds out a battered top hat and a bottle to you. "Quack doctor," he says. "Bring him back to life."
text [87aae5] = 哑剧艺人们穿着纸条做的戏服来到小路边的农场：一个骑士、一条龙、一个国王，还有一个拿剑的人不停地把所有人杀掉。按规矩，医生总是从观众里找。一个艺人把一顶破礼帽和一个瓶子递给你。“江湖郎中，”他说，“把他救活。”
# en: A farmyard in winter lit by lanterns, mummers in costumes made of paper strips, their faces hidden behind paper fringes, performing a play, a knight lying on the ground, a student being handed a doctor's top hat and a bottle.
scene [34707d] = 灯笼照亮的冬日农家院子，穿着纸条戏服、脸藏在纸穗后面的哑剧艺人在演戏，一个骑士躺在地上，有人把一顶医生的礼帽和一个瓶子递给一个学生。
# en: Play the Doctor
opt.left.label [d7293b] = 演医生
# en: You doff the hat, uncork the bottle and declare your cures, louder and sillier with every line, and pour a drop in the knight's mouth, and he leaps up to a great cheer. The mummers make you come with them to three more farms.
opt.left.say.1 [2f2bd3] = 你脱帽致意，拔开瓶塞，宣讲你的灵丹妙药，一句比一句响、一句比一句傻，往骑士嘴里倒了一滴，他一跃而起，满场欢呼。艺人们非拉着你跟他们再去三家农场。
# en: You forget the lines, and the ones you make up don't rhyme, and the knight has to bring himself back to life out of pity. The yard is kind about it. Nobody asks you to the next farm.
opt.left.say.2 [bb117e] = 你忘了台词，编出来的又不押韵，骑士出于同情只好自己活了过来。院子里的人很宽容。没人请你去下一家农场。
# en: Put a coin in the hat
opt.right.label [88f9cf] = 往帽子里放枚硬币
# en: You put a coin in the hat to be let off, and watch from the back while the farmer's wife plays the Doctor instead, far better than you would have. The dragon gives you a paper strip off its tail.
opt.right.say.1 [7f6aee] = 你往帽子里放了一枚硬币好免了这差事，站在后面看农夫的妻子替你演医生，比你演得好多了。那条龙从尾巴上扯下一根纸条送给你。

@event lanes_signpost
# en: The Turned Signpost
title [88471d] = 被转过的路标
# en: The fingerpost at the crossroads has been twisted round on its post, so the market village is up the farm track and the mill is in a pond. From behind the wall comes a lot of giggling. A carter has just taken the wrong road and is coming back, swearing.
text [877db3] = 十字路口的指路牌被人在柱子上转了个向，于是集镇在农场小道上头，磨坊在池塘里。墙后传来一阵阵咯咯笑。一个车夫刚走错了路，正骂骂咧咧地往回赶。
# en: A country crossroads, an old wooden fingerpost signpost twisted round on its post so its arms point the wrong ways, two young farmhands giggling behind a wall, a student looking up at it.
scene [423d8c] = 乡间十字路口，一根老木指路牌在柱子上被转了向，指向全错，两个年轻的雇工躲在墙后咯咯笑，一个学生抬头看着它。
# en: Turn it back the right way
opt.left.label [058254] = 把它转回原位
# en: You put your shoulder to the post and heave it round, rasping your palms, while the farmhands behind the wall groan. The carter thanks you, and then goes and tells their foreman, which you hadn't meant at all.
opt.left.say.1 [dc6087] = 你用肩膀顶住柱子把它扳了回来，手掌磨得生疼，墙后的雇工们一阵哀叹。车夫谢了你，然后跑去告诉了他们的工头，这可完全不是你的本意。
# en: Follow it anyway, for fun
opt.right.label [dc8ad0] = 偏照着它走，图个乐
# en: You follow the sign to the market village, up the farm track, over two fields, round a pond, and come out, astonishingly, at the market village, the long way. The farmhands follow you to see. Your boots are full of mud and your legs are done.
opt.right.say.1 [744c06] = 你照着牌子往集镇走，上了农场小道，穿过两块田，绕过一个池塘，居然真的走到了集镇，绕了远路。雇工们跟在后面来看。你的靴子里灌满了泥，腿也走废了。

@event lanes_rainbow
# en: Where the Rainbow Ends
title [98eb15] = 彩虹的尽头
# en: A shower comes over and goes, and behind it there's a rainbow so bright it looks painted, coming down, quite plainly, into the next field but one. Two dairymaids are already running for it. "There's gold!" one shouts back at you. "Under the end! Everyone knows!"
text [75b8ad] = 一阵阵雨过去，后面出现一道彩虹，亮得像画上去的，明明白白地落进隔一块的那片田里。两个挤奶女工已经朝它跑去了。“那儿有金子！”一个回头冲你喊，“就在尽头下面！谁都知道！”
# en: A wet country lane after a shower, a vivid rainbow coming down into a field a little way off, two dairymaids running towards it, a student watching.
scene [d8b375] = 阵雨过后湿漉漉的乡间小路，一道鲜艳的彩虹落进不远处的一片田里，两个挤奶女工朝它跑去，一个学生在看。
# en: Run for the end with them
opt.left.label [160ac5] = 跟他们一起去追尽头
# en: You run with them through two wet fields, and the end of the rainbow keeps exactly one field ahead, and then fades out over a pond. The dairymaids are disgusted. You're soaked to the knees, and laughing so hard you have to sit down on a wet stile.
opt.left.say.1 [5a2814] = 你和她们跑过两片湿田，彩虹的尽头始终在前面一块田外，然后在一个池塘上方淡去了。挤奶女工们大失所望。你湿到膝盖，笑得只好在一个湿漉漉的栅栏台阶上坐下。
# en: Stay and watch it from the lane
opt.right.label [63d5e8] = 留在路上看它
# en: You lean on the gate and watch it fade, band by band, the red going last. A shepherd going by tells you, quite seriously, that there's a rainbow over that field most wet days and nobody's ever got to the end of it. Your boots are full of water from the lane.
opt.right.say.1 [c0f7dc] = 你靠着门看它一道一道地淡去，红色最后消失。一个路过的牧羊人非常认真地告诉你，下雨的日子那片田上多半都有彩虹，从没人走到过它的尽头。你的靴子里灌满了路上的水。

@event lanes_lost_walker
# en: The Wrong Map
title [8d8963] = 错误的地图
# en: A tall man in brand-new walking tweeds is standing in the lane with an enormous map, turning it round and round. He's come up from the capital on the coach to see the view from the ridge, he says, and the map says the ridge is exactly where he's standing, in a ditch.
text [57f6d1] = 一个穿着崭新徒步花呢衣服的高个子男人站在小路上，捧着一张巨大的地图转来转去。他说他从首都坐马车上来，想看看山脊上的风景，而地图说山脊就在他站的地方，在一条沟里。
# en: A country lane, a tall man in tweeds and walking boots from the city holding a large unfolded map upside down, looking lost, a student pointing the right way.
scene [d8316d] = 乡间小路，一个穿花呢衣服和徒步靴的城里高个子倒拿着一张摊开的大地图，一脸迷茫，一个学生在给他指路。
# en: Walk him to the ridge path
opt.left.label [bd5c2a] = 送他到山脊小径
# en: You walk him the two miles to the ridge path and point him up it. He insists on paying you for the trouble, very formally, and strides off up the hill with his map upside down again. Your feet feel the extra miles.
opt.left.say.1 [0bb481] = 你陪他走了两英里到山脊小径，指他往上走。他坚持要付你辛苦费，非常郑重，然后又把地图倒拿着大步上山了。多走的路让你的脚吃不消。
# en: Correct his map for him
opt.right.label [a0dcde] = 替他改正地图
# en: You borrow his pencil and draw the real lanes on his map, and he argues with every line: the map was very expensive. In the end he goes the way the map says. You see him an hour later, from the ridge, still in the ditch.
opt.right.say.1 [a810cd] = 你借了他的铅笔，在他地图上画出真正的小路，他每一笔都要争：这地图很贵。最后他还是照着地图走了。一个钟头后你从山脊上看见他，还在那条沟里。

@event lanes_hayrick
# en: The Hayrick
title [d66279] = 干草垛
# en: There's a new hayrick in the field by the lane, tall as a cottage and still warm through, smelling of summer, with the farmer's ladder left against its side. Nobody's about. The whole afternoon is lying there, unclaimed.
text [f2f9d4] = 小路边的田里有个新干草垛，像小屋那么高，里头还暖着，一股夏天的味道，农夫的梯子靠在一边。四下没人。整个下午就那么躺在那里，没人认领。
# en: A tall golden hayrick in a summer field by a lane, a ladder against its side, a student lying on top in the sun with the whole valley spread out below.
scene [aa709f] = 夏日小路边田里一个高高的金色干草垛，一架梯子靠在旁边，一个学生躺在垛顶晒太阳，整个山谷铺展在下面。
# en: Climb up and sleep in the sun
opt.left.label [27419d] = 爬上去晒着太阳睡觉
# en: You climb up and lie on the top in the sweet hay and are asleep in a minute. You wake an hour later with the sun gone round, the back of your neck burnt red and hay in every seam you own.
opt.left.say.1 [b4d8e2] = 你爬上去躺在垛顶香甜的干草里，一分钟就睡着了。一个钟头后醒来，太阳已经转了过去，你的后颈晒得通红，身上每一道缝里都是干草。
# en: Climb up and look at the valley
opt.right.label [cac420] = 爬上去看看山谷
# en: From the top you can see the whole valley at once: both villages, the mill race, the ford, the moor's dark edge, the road you came in by. You sit and learn it like a map until the farmer comes and shouts you down, very rudely.
opt.right.say.1 [7b258c] = 从顶上你能一眼看遍整个山谷：两个村子、磨坊水渠、渡口、荒原黑沉沉的边缘、你来时的路。你坐在那儿像背地图一样把它记熟，直到农夫过来，非常粗鲁地把你吼下来。

@event lanes_fallen_tree
# en: The Tree Across the Lane
title [056c4c] = 横在路上的树
# en: Last night's gale has brought a great ash down across the lane, roots and all, and a carter's milk cart is stuck behind it, the churns going warm. The carter has a bow saw and a look of a man facing a day's work. "Unless," he says, looking at your scarf, "you know a trick."
text [6d7b18] = 昨夜的大风把一棵大白蜡树连根刮倒，横在小路上，一个车夫的运奶车被堵在后面，奶桶正在变温。车夫拿着一把弓锯，一副面对一整天活计的表情。“除非，”他看着你的围巾说，“你会点什么把戏。”
# en: A country lane completely blocked by a huge fallen ash tree after a gale, a carter's cart stuck behind it, the carter with a bow saw, a student looking at the trunk.
scene [c7d2d3] = 大风过后，一条乡间小路被一棵倒下的巨大白蜡树完全堵住，一个车夫的车卡在后面，车夫拿着弓锯，一个学生看着树干。
# en: Take the other end of the saw
opt.left.label [f76371] = 拉锯子的另一头
# en: You saw for two hours, turn and turn about, till the trunk is in three pieces and the two of you can roll the middle one into the ditch. The carter shares his bread and cheese. You have blisters on both palms.
opt.left.say.1 [d1a483] = 你们轮流锯了两个钟头，把树干锯成三截，两人合力把中间那截滚进沟里。车夫分了你面包和奶酪。你两只手掌都磨出了水泡。
# en: Shift it with a spell
opt.right.label [04dcb5] = 用法术挪开它
# en: You set your feet and lift, and the whole trunk rolls slowly over, groaning, and settles in the ditch with its roots in the air. The carter takes his hat off to you and drives on without a word, which in the valley is a great compliment.
opt.right.say.1 [1dcae1] = 你站稳脚跟一抬，整根树干慢慢翻了过去，嘎吱作响，根朝天地落进沟里。车夫向你脱帽致意，一言不发地赶车走了，在山谷里这是极高的称赞。
# en: The trunk shifts, slides and settles back, harder, onto your end of the lane, pinning your coat. The carter saws you free, very patient about it, and then saws the tree. It takes the rest of the day and you're scraped and filthy.
opt.right.say.2 [2e2160] = 树干动了动，滑了滑，又更重地落回你这头的路上，压住了你的外套。车夫非常耐心地把你锯了出来，然后锯树。这花了剩下的一整天，你浑身擦伤、一身脏。
